From 14ce398fba54b8edfd6cf60634e9a02415911df7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex <alexsbryan@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 12:40:22 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] fix: drop the unit from minutes written as '50 min'

Production: 3 of 30 notes (input.ref 7f30b7118961, 451520f309d7,
3d0c98f71318) get 422 from the clearinghouse (/service/effects). The
instrumentation trials (instrument-failures@26ec1f2, @2e80f9d) show the
rejected claims differ from the 22 accepted ones only in minutes:
claim.minutes.form len 10 (non_digits) vs len 6 (digits);
minutes.is.digits_space_min = yes, has.letter = yes, has.space = yes; and the
rejection's own words name minutes (reject.says.minutes = yes, every other
field no; keys code and error).

notes.minutes keeps the digits when the value is digits plus min/mins/minutes,
and passes every other form on as written, as before.

Test: tests/test_notes.py Minutes (fixture fixtures/minutes-with-unit.txt,
synthetic) fails on main (1 failure, 1 error) and passes here.
