From eac85bae96bce159f9ffb8a9282a26958809b019 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex <alexsbryan@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 12:43:11 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix: read a service date written as 'Nov 3, 2026 -
 remark'

Production: 3 of 30 notes (input.ref ee11d561ad0e, 194941a5fabf,
26edf09a60c2) end in ValueError at notes.py:23 (strptime '%Y-%m-%d').
Instrumentation trials on instrument-failures (@26ec1f2, @2e80f9d, @6210e13,
@ee1242b) show, for exactly those three: parse.date_form = has_letters,
error_form = does_not_match; the date starts with a month abbreviation, has
one four-digit year, no ISO date, no weekday, is over 35 characters, and
splits at ' - ' into a head that parses as '%b %d, %Y'
(date.head.parses_as.abbr_month_d_comma_y = yes) and a tail with a comma,
no digit and no month word.

notes.service_date tries ISO, then the part before ' - ' as '%b %d, %Y' or
'%B %d, %Y'. Every other form still raises ValueError, as before.

Test: tests/test_notes.py ServiceDate (fixture
fixtures/date-written-with-remark.txt, synthetic) fails on main (3 errors)
and passes here.
---
 fixtures/date-written-with-remark.txt |  7 +++++++
 notes.py                              | 21 ++++++++++++++++++++-
 tests/test_notes.py                   | 14 ++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 41 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 fixtures/date-written-with-remark.txt

